#### 9. Dimensions of Base & Derived Quantities
* Fundamental quantities have their own primary dimensions: \\([M^1], [L^1], [T^1], [I^1], [K^1], [\text{mol}^1], [\text{cd}^1]\\).
* The dimension of any base quantity in any other base quantity is strictly **zero** (e.g., mass has zero dimension in length, time, etc.).
* Supplementary quantities (radian, steradian) have **zero dimensions in all base quantities**.

---

