#### 12. Applications
1. **Coherent System of Units:** SI is a **coherent system**, meaning derived units are obtained by simple multiplication and division of base units without introducing numerical multiplying factors [21–22].
2. **Standardization in Engineering & Industry:** Ensures inter-compatibility of scientific data, manufacturing dimensions, and electrical standards globally.

---

#### 13. Important H.C. Verma Concepts
* **Non-Uniqueness of Base Quantities (HCV Sec 1.3):** The choice of base quantities is not unique. Different systems can select different sets of quantities as base quantities.
* **Condition for an Invalid Base Set (HCV Ch 1, Obj I Q1):** A set of physical quantities **CANNOT** be chosen as a set of fundamental quantities if any one of them can be derived from the others.
  * *Example:* The set \\((\text{Length}, \text{Time}, \text{Velocity})\\) **cannot** form a base set because \\(\text{Velocity} = \frac{\text{Length}}{\text{Time}}\\).
  * The set \\((\text{Length}, \text{Mass}, \text{Velocity})\\) **can** form a valid base set because Mass is independent of Length and Velocity.

---

#### 14. Common Confusions

| Concept A | Concept B | APPSC Distinction & Trap |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Base Unit** | **Derived Unit** | Base units are independently defined; derived units are formed by combining base units. |
| **Base Set \\((\text{L}, \text{T}, \text{V})\\)** | **Base Set \\((\text{M}, \text{L}, \text{V})\\)** | \\((\text{L}, \text{T}, \text{V})\\) is **invalid** because \\(V = L/T\\). \\((\text{M}, \text{L}, \text{V})\\) is **valid** because \\(M\\) cannot be formed from \\(L\\) and \\(V\\). |
| **Radian (\\(\text{rad}\\))** | **Radian Dimension** | Radian is a **unit**, but its dimensional formula is \\([M^0 L^0 T^0]\\). |

